There is a legend in Astra town. On the night of the new moon, people in town who are about to die will turn into flowers. The flowers in the town are all silver, just like a few stars scattered on the earth.

Once, I asked an elder if the legend is true. He didn't answer. He was silent and looked up at the stars. For a long time, he read a poem:

Youth passes as a fleeting river, star lies in the silver flower.














































