Even if I work in a foreign land now, I still think of the flowers in the town. Five trivial petals surround the alabastrum, like a silver bell lying on the ground. The flower will only open on the night of the new moon. On other days, the bridal flowers are like maiden sleeping deeply.

When I was still young, I had been to an empty house in town. The wooden door with lucid texture，the rough desk covered with dust, they all show that there had been no one living here for a long time. In the back yard, all the weeds were dead, there was only a silver flower alive.





