That day, my younger sister suddenly called me and told me that she had been having the same dream. She said she dreamed about the flowers in town. At first, it was only on the night of the new moon that she had such a dream. Later, it became more and more frequent. In the dream, those flowers bloom without exception. The sky is like ink. In the night with only a few stars, silver flowers twinkle on the ground, which makes her feel inexplicable fear.

I didn't pay too much attention on it then. But now I feel regret for it.

A week after the call, my sister fainted on the road. She was sent to the hospital immediately. The hospital gave her a physical examination. She was found to have advanced gastric cancer. I told the situation of my sister to the whole family. Everyone kept silent, because our family cannot afford the expensive medical expenses.






