I look into the room. My sister has stood up.



 I cry, trying to hug her.

I touch her body, and find out that her body is cold as ice. Tears come out from her eyes again. The blue eyes of my sister is shining, so lucid, they reflect all the stars in the sky.

Everything around me starts to get distorted. The whole room is surrounded by silvery, I am densed in the silver world, my mind is gradually swallowed by silver.

I reach out my hand, but they go straight through my sister's body. Looking down, I only have a silver petal in my hand. The petal is warm, like first rays of the morning sun. The silvery around retreat in a sudden, everything restores slient. I look at my sister

Sister? Isn't me the only child in my family?

I look at the photo of my family. On the picture, my father is smiling, hugging me when I was young with my mother. Beside my mother, it's an empty baby carriage.

That's right, there are only three people in my family.

In this silent night, the stars are clearly visible in the sky. The flowers in town are blooming, embellishing the small town.

Youth passes as a fleeting river, star lies in the silver flower.

I pick up a fallen petal. Beneath the silver, I see all the stars.







                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
